<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port Phillip District</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1836–1851</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Port Phillip District was an administrative district of the colony of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> covering present-day Victoria, from 1836 to 1851. Centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melbourne">Melbourne</a>, it was governed from 1839 by a superintendent, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-la-trobe">Charles La Trobe</a>. Its settlers campaigned for separation from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a>, and in July 1851 it became the separate colony of Victoria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-phillip-district.jpg" alt="Port Phillip District" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stephen Bain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Phillip_District_location_map_1839.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
